=== SURVEY ===

--- Baseline route + page (must remain canonical when ai_mode='off') ---
Backend: POST /api/v1/trip-planner/plan wired through
  internal/api/router.go → tripPlannerHandler.PlanTrip →
  internal/api/trip_planner_handler.go (existing). The heuristic
  computePlan() does:
    1. Estimate consumption from user history (kWhPer100km) with a
       Tesla-vehicle-specific fallback.
    2. Pick top-N candidate SuperCharger stops along the great-circle
       corridor.
    3. Build a per-leg drive segment + charge segment plan with an
       SOC curve, ETA, energy, and cost.
    4. Return a tripPlanResponse envelope containing route +
       remainingSOC + warnings.

  This is the canonical baseline. It MUST remain visible and clickable
  for users with ai_mode='off' and is NOT touched by this slice.

Frontend page: web/src/features/driving/pages/TripPlannerPage.tsx
  - Uses usePlanTrip() mutation → POST /api/v1/trip-planner/plan
  - Renders: Plan form (origin / destination / SOC / minArrivalSOC /
    speedFactor) + StatCards (distance / duration / energy / cost) +
    TripPlannerMap + SOCRouteChart + TripLegList + AlertBanner for
    warnings.
  - No `if (aiEnabled) replace(...)` branches. The AI surface is added
    as a NEW <FadeIn>-wrapped panel ABOVE the form, conditionally
    rendered by withAiFeature('trip-planner-llm-agent', …) so the
    baseline form stays canonical.

--- DTOs / shapes ---
api.tripPlanRequest (from internal/api/trip_planner_handler.go):
  Origin TripLocation, Destination TripLocation, CurrentSOC float64,
  MinArrivalSOC float64, SpeedFactor float64, VehicleID int64.

api.tripPlanResponse (from internal/api/trip_planner_handler.go):
  Route TripRoute, ChargeStops []ChargeStop, SOCCurve []SOCPoint,
  EstimatedEnergyWh float64, EstimatedCost float64, Warnings []string,
  RemainingSOC float64.

Frontend types in web/src/types/driving.ts (TripPlanRequest +
TripPlan) mirror these snake_case fields.

