The Go-side test exercises the load-bearing AI-off contract by
constructing a chi router with the same /api/v1/ai mount that
production uses, with ai_mode='off' set on the request context.
It asserts:
  (a) POST /api/v1/ai/trips/plan/draft returns 404 with no headers
      leaking the existence of the route.
  (b) POST /api/v1/trip-planner/plan returns 200 with a
      tripPlanResponse envelope including a "surface" marker
      equal to "baseline_heuristic_trip_planner", proving the
      baseline handler ran end-to-end. This is the "uses heuristic
      planner" semantic in the test name.

The React-side test exercises the corresponding UI invariant — the
AI surface is absent from the DOM in off mode + present only when
both gates are open.

